  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 14 actions (analogway_midra.js:193-655, one object literal in init_actions) and no feedbacks (the module defines none and never calls setFeedbackDefinitions).",
    "Protocol: Analog Way text protocol over TCP port 10500 (hard-coded, analogway_midra.js:33) to the config host; config also has a 'variant' dropdown (Eikos2, Saphyr, Pulse2, SmartMatriX2, QuickMatriX, QuickVu and the -H variants) that is not used by the actions. The module's sendcmd sends the command text without appending a line terminator (analogway_midra.js:658-676), unlike the LiveCore module.",
    "Actions that use the shared actionCallback take their action id as the command id and build the command from options with ids '0'..'5' (sent in order, each followed by a comma) and 'value'. Their option ids are therefore protocol positions, not names.",
    "All dropdown ids are strings; screens are S1/S2 ('0'/'1'), inputs 1-10 are ids '0'-'9' (zero-based, labels 1-10). Layer ids '0'-'7' (Background, PiP 1-4, Logo 1-2, Audio).",
    "Memory numbers are entered 1-based (1-8) in the textinput, with leading zeros allowed, and the callback subtracts 1.",
    "Tooltips in the source are recorded as `description`. The action-level tooltips of Quick Frame and Preview Layer are in the entity description.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.4.1: options do not support expressions. Variables and presets are not defined by this module."
  ]
}
